## Conclusion

What seems like an instant and trivial action — typing a URL and pressing Enter — is actually the result of an intricate, highly optimized chain of systems working in perfect coordination. Understanding this flow is foundational for any software engineer, whether you work on the front end, the back end, or infrastructure.

Mastering this question isn't just about acing interviews. It's about understanding the web as a system — and that understanding makes you a better engineer at every layer.

